  "_how_to_update": [
    "This file is the only place the pricing page's competitor figures live.",
    "To correct one: edit it below, set that row's last_verified to the date you checked its",
    "source URL, set status to 'verified' (you fetched it today) or 'single-fetch' (one check,",
    "not re-confirmed since), and redeploy fancier's assets. The running page re-fetches this",
    "file on load, so an asset deploy is enough -- no Rust rebuild. A rebuild only refreshes",
    "the pre-JavaScript copy baked into the prerendered HTML.",
    "A figure older than stale_after_days renders with a visible 'recheck' cue.",
    "Keep notes to ONE sentence. This is the page that has to explain why someone should choose",
    "us, and text nobody reads persuades nobody: a note's job is the single key difference, what a",
    "vendor does not do or why they legitimately beat us.",
    "ONE deliberate exception, do not trim it: Golioth is the only competitor that genuinely beats",
    "us on price across our own self-serve band, so their row carries the crossover numbers and the",
    "three things they lack. Losing that would make the page dishonest, not shorter.",
    "choose us, and text nobody reads persuades nobody. The note's job is the single key",
    "difference: what a vendor does not do, or why they legitimately beat us.",
    "A row with no entry under a column renders as 'not published'; a row with no figures at",
    "all is status 'unpriced'. Never a guessed number in either case.",
    "build_your_own is raw infrastructure. It stays OUT of the table on purpose: a rate in",
    "cents sitting in a price column anchors a reader before any feature list reaches them.",
    "Figures come from pidgeiot-business/pricing-analysis-2026-08.md sections 1.8 and 1.9."
